WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.260
Luton, 2015.

2
00:00:02.310 --> 00:00:07.770
93,500 people aged 16 to 64 are in work.

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:13.190
A decade later, in the year
from July 2025 to June 2026,

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.270
the figure is 96,500.

5
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.990
That's three thousand more people in work.

6
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.970
But the estimated employment rate,
the share of that age group in work,

7
00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:27.850
fell from 67.8 per cent to 66.5 per cent.

8
00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:30.490
More workers, a lower rate.

9
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.830
So is Luton doing better, or worse?

10
00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:37.210
In this mission, you'll test
claims of success with jobs,

11
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.670
pay, deprivation and
life expectancy figures.

12
00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.910
Then you'll weigh how
to measure integration,

13
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.430
from voter turnout to hate crime
figures that need careful reading.

14
00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:50.870
Your mission: judge whether
Luton is doing better or worse,

15
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.470
and justify the measures you use.
